                      (        forth.asm):03689         * Double (numerator high/low) gets divided by a single cell number. Please note
                      (        forth.asm):03690         * that this is a strictly unsigned business. Input parameters are supposed to
                      (        forth.asm):03691         * have been set up by the caller on the system stack. The quotient (high/low)
                      (        forth.asm):03692         * and remainder are returned the same way. Current users of this routine are
                      (        forth.asm):03693         * CVT (#) and UMSLMOD (UM/MOD).
                      (        forth.asm):03694         *
                      (        forth.asm):03695         * Stack structure:
                      (        forth.asm):03696         * ,s    Return address          16 bits
                      (        forth.asm):03697         * 2,s   Remainder               16 bits
                      (        forth.asm):03698         * 4,s   Bitmask high            16 bits
                      (        forth.asm):03699         * 6,s   Bitmask low             16 bits
                      (        forth.asm):03700         * 8,s   Quotient high           16 bits
                      (        forth.asm):03701         * 10,s  Quotient low            16 bits
                      (        forth.asm):03702         * 12,s  Numerator high          16 bits
                      (        forth.asm):03703         * 14,s  Numerator low           16 bits
                      (        forth.asm):03704         * 16,s  Denominator             16 bits
                      (        forth.asm):03705         * 18,s  Remainder carry         8 bits
                      (        forth.asm):03706         *
