                      (        forth.asm):04140         * The algorithm implemented here is similar to Donald's Knuth algorithm M,
                      (        forth.asm):04141         * as described in "The Art of Computer Programming", Volume II, 3rd edition,
                      (        forth.asm):04142         * section 4.3.1, pp 268. It is not as generic as algorithm M but fits our
                      (        forth.asm):04143         * particular purpose here: a 16x16 bit unsigned multiplication that yields
                      (        forth.asm):04144         * a 32 bit result. A simpler description of algorithm M can be found in
                      (        forth.asm):04145         * Henry S. Warren Junior's "Hacker's Delight", second edition, section 8-1,
                      (        forth.asm):04146         * pp 171. A C prototype implementation for a little endian host is provided
                      (        forth.asm):04147         * in SW/util/umstar.c.
                      (        forth.asm):04148         * In essence we reduce the problem to a 2 digit by 2 digit (expressed in
                      (        forth.asm):04149         * base 256) multiplication and use the 6809 MUL (A * B -> D) instruction.
F99E 03               (        forth.asm):04150         UMSTAR  fcb     3               ANSI (Core)
F99F 554D2A           (        forth.asm):04151                 fcc     'UM*'           ( u1 u2 -- ud )
F9A2 F993             (        forth.asm):04152                 fdb     MSTAR
                      (        forth.asm):04153                 RFCS
F9A4 BDEA22           (        forth.asm):04154 (7)             jsr     MIN2PST         2 parameters need to be stacked up
                      (        forth.asm):04155         * Register allocation notes:
                      (        forth.asm):04156         * X: pointer to ud1 (ARG_U/p in the C code).
                      (        forth.asm):04157         * Y: pointer to ud2 (ARG_V/q in the C code).
                      (        forth.asm):04158         * E: Inner loop index (i in the C code).
                      (        forth.asm):04159         * F: Outer loop index (j in the C code).
                      (        forth.asm):04160         *
                      (        forth.asm):04161         * We save U to the system stack and use it to point to a scratch area allocated
                      (        forth.asm):04162         * from the system stack that will contain the 4 bytes (double cell) ultimately
                      (        forth.asm):04163         * holding the result (MSB first, what else?).
                      (        forth.asm):04164         *
                      (        forth.asm):04165         * System stack structure:
                      (        forth.asm):04166         * ,S    Result scratch area (Result MSB)
                      (        forth.asm):04167         * 2,S   Result scratch area (Result LSB)
                      (        forth.asm):04168         * 4,S   Saved U register
                      (        forth.asm):04169         * Total: 6 bytes.
F9A7 327A             (        forth.asm):04170 (4+1)           leas    -6,s            Allocate system stack scratch space
